      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For writing purposes, observational comedy often works by examining exaggerated social archetypes or ingrained biases people readily notice in daily life. Writers might look at broad behavioral patterns, media portrayals, or cultural habits as starting points for satire. Instead of focusing on stereotypes, you could lean into universal human experiences like routines, family dynamics, or cultural clashes to build comedic tension. Exploring these areas allows for critique without relying on damaging generalizations.",
